---
title: Headless {js} executed-output
---

A document a headless agent runs `taliesin read --run` against to confirm its `{js}`
cells actually produced browser output. `{js}` runs in the browser (not on a kernel),
so `read --run` drives a local headless Chrome over the built page and reports, per
cell, whether an `<svg>`/`<canvas>` painted, `[js error: …]` when the cell threw, or
`skipped` when no Chrome is available. Observation-only: no reactive re-run, no source
or `_freeze` write.

An Observable Plot cell that paints an `<svg>`:

```{js}
return Plot.plot({
  width: 320,
  height: 200,
  marks: [Plot.dot([[0, 0], [1, 1], [2, 4], [3, 9]])],
});
```

A deliberately-throwing cell, to pin the `[js error: …]` projection:

```{js}
throw new Error("intentional read --run test failure");
```
